    description: "WHY. The full suite runs at 01:00 and 13:00 UTC, so a break can wait up to 12 hours before anything measures it. Twice daily was set when every PR ran its whole selection; a run after every merge was removed because with 20 or more merges a day and one run at a time the queue never cleared.\n\nWHAT (owner ruling: measure, then propose; it stays twice daily meanwhile). Measure from Woodpecker's pipeline records: how long a full run and a nightly take; how long the runner sits idle per day; how long a PR's CI takes BEFORE its first test starts (container, install, grammar build). Then bring the owner ONE proposed schedule. The schedule lives in Woodpecker's repository settings; only the owner can change it.\n\nALSO FROM THIS MEASUREMENT. Whether a CI wall-time target can be stated at all (the owner ruled: no CI target until this is known).\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. The three measurements with the pipelines they came from; the proposal posted to the owner; the item moves to needs_human_review until the owner rules.\n\nSOURCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md; the owner's rulings of 2026-11-17 are its second 'Made' table. Measurements: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_followup_11172026/README.md, slice_graph_11152026/README.md, stale_graph_1a_11152026/README.md, fast_smart_test_11152026/README.md (the 37-PR replay)."  # 778e
    fields: {}  # 778e
