  clock: 4  # cddd
  nonce: cddd  # cddd
  message: "MEASURED (2026-11-19 00:30 UTC; PR #2265 adds 'ci-debug pipelines'; data and analysis in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/cadence/README.md). 2,000 Woodpecker pipelines 10-01..11-19. Last 14 days: full suite median 38.5-40.1 min (n=25; 3 more killed at the 60-min limit); nightly 108.5 min (n=12); PR pipeline 3.6 min median, p90 19.1. Runner busy 3.5-8.6 h/day, IDLE 15.4-20.5 h/day; at most 2 pipelines at once every day; queue wait median 0.0 min (worst PR 104.9 min, once). A PR's setup before its first test: pytest step starts a median 100 s into the pipeline, then 47-66 s of installs (8 logs): about 2.5 min per PR. Crons fire 01:0x and 13:0x (full suite), 05:3x (nightly, ends about 07:20); merges land at every UTC hour.\nTHE ONE PROPOSAL FOR THE OWNER: full suite at 01:00, 09:00, 13:00, 17:00, 21:00 UTC ('0 1,9,13,17,21 * * *'), nightly unchanged. A break waits at most 4 h by day, 8 h overnight (today up to 12 h). Cost: 3 more 40-min runs, about 2 runner-hours a day on a runner idle 15-20 h a day; 05:00 is skipped so a full run never shares the agent's two slots with the nightly. Watch after the change: PR queue wait (it is 0 today; a full run holds one of the two slots for 40 min). Only the owner can change the schedule (Woodpecker repository settings)."  # cddd
- op: discuss  # 67c1
